is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ Then, the sample variance ${S}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{S}^{2}=\\frac{1}{n-1}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{({X}_{i}-\\overset{―}{X})}^{2}=\\frac{n}{n-1}[\\overset{―}{{X}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{X})}^{2}].\n$$\n\nNote that:\n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the sample mean,\n\n- the sample variance ${S}^{2}$ is an unbiased estimator of the population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ and\n\n- ${\\overset{^}{\\sigma }}^{2}={s}^{2}$ denotes an unbiased estimate of ${\\sigma }^{2}$ that's computed from the sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}.$\n\nHere, there are $n=50$ data points in the sample, and we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}=147.\n$$\n\nTherefore, an unbiased estimate of the population variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{^}{\\sigma }}^{2} & ={s}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{n}{n-1}[\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{50}{50-1}\\cdot 147 \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\,350}{49} \\\\  & =150.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184870 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184194 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "897ae010-a9a2-5971-a1ec-c2618cb8ad2c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Population Variance From Sample Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba80ffcf-73eb-5f1a-8fd4-d63450f1bfa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183830} {:answer/id #uuid "e450345a-e368-5b38-aab7-b820247601a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183831} {:answer/id #uuid "e8b6517e-8f2a-5f23-8e22-b1018a73b77c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183832} {:answer/id #uuid "18814d35-1a72-50a7-a1ca-7d133e3fff5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183833} {:answer/id #uuid "67109040-4d97-57d2-9184-2956dfd755e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8b6517e-8f2a-5f23-8e22-b1018a73b77c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183832} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf68f810-83c4-5c31-ab5d-3a95adffba29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183829}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0fd4e806-e213-5cdb-aa92-418bede47190" :question/math-academy-id "q-88857" :question/problem "Suppose the following data is sampled from a population. Compute an unbiased estimate of the population variance.\n\n$$\n4,\\,8,\\,10,\\,6,\\,7\n$$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ Then, the sample variance ${S}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{S}^{2}=\\frac{1}{n-1}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{({X}_{i}-\\overset{―}{X})}^{2}=\\frac{n}{n-1}[\\overset{―}{{X}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{X})}^{2}].\n$$\n\nNote that:\n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the sample mean,\n\n- the sample variance ${S}^{2}$ is an unbiased estimator of the population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ and\n\n- ${\\overset{^}{\\sigma }}^{2}={s}^{2}$ denotes the unbiased estimate of ${\\sigma }^{2}$ computed from the sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}.$\n\nFirst, we will compute the quantity\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe proceed as follows:\n\n- The mean of the data is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{5}(4+8+10+6+7) \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{5} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The mean of the squared data is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{5}({4}^{2}+{8}^{2}+{10}^{2}+{6}^{2}+{7}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{265}{5} \\\\  & =53.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2} & =53-{7}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the sample variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{^}{\\sigma }}^{2} & ={s}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{n}{n-1}[\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{5-1}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, an unbiased estimate of the population variance is $5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443484 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184195 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb182688-828c-5252-8d6d-d09c93ba2bc8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Estimate of the Population Variance Using the Alternative Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28bebf10-4736-5d5b-991d-68bf2ddce06d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443419} {:answer/id #uuid "4a233216-fa1d-56d4-9e2b-16a571302e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443423} {:answer/id #uuid "5b23c34b-b69a-57c5-b7e6-fd2318116de7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443428} {:answer/id #uuid "b44643ad-4dc5-5500-9ce5-ee71edf17395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443445} {:answer/id #uuid "c69748ac-f398-5d94-96ca-00128cc3c702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443449}] :a