e of ${\\sigma }^{2}$ that's computed from the sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}.$\n\nHere, there are $n=26$ data points in the sample, and we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, an unbiased estimate of the population variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{^}{\\sigma }}^{2} & ={s}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{n}{n-1}[\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{26-1}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{130}{25} \\\\  & =5.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443488 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184194 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "897ae010-a9a2-5971-a1ec-c2618cb8ad2c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Population Variance From Sample Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15c9d4c7-4932-51cb-851e-20bc41eff0b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443414} {:answer/id #uuid "6d11e664-ae79-5311-b5f7-4596a10ca2c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443433} {:answer/id #uuid "cf6f6514-8524-5db9-8a22-6714044d22e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443451} {:answer/id #uuid "ed063622-78e8-5cc4-9cae-11117d2078f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443460} {:answer/id #uuid "fb745932-05e5-5ac3-8346-680974ad3332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb745932-05e5-5ac3-8346-680974ad3332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443465} :answer-field/id #uuid "88e4a68e-c7a0-55f8-9072-f9288e94c7b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-fi